.SS "int wget_xml_parse_buffer (const char * buf, wget_xml_callback * callback, void * user_ctx, int hints)"

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIbuf\fP Zero-terminated XML or HTML input data 
.br
\fIcallback\fP Function called for each token scan result 
.br
\fIuser_ctx\fP User-defined context variable, handed to \fRcallback\fP 
.br
\fIhints\fP Flags to influence parsing
.RE
.PP
This function scans the XML input from \fRbuf\fP and calls \fRcallback\fP for each token found\&. \fRuser_ctx\fP is a user-defined context variable and given to each call of \fRcallback\fP\&.

.PP
\fRhints\fP may be 0 or any combination of XML_HINT_REMOVE_EMPTY_CONTENT and XML_HINT_HTML\&.

.PP
XML_HINT_REMOVE_EMPTY_CONTENT reduces the number of calls to \fRcallback\fP by ignoring empty content and superfluous spaces\&.

.PP
XML_HINT_HTML turns on HTML scanning\&. 
.SS "void wget_html_parse_buffer (const char * buf, wget_xml_callback * callback, void * user_ctx, int hints)"

